## Search-term bias caught, 19 Aug
Initial hand-collection search terms were skewed toward size and fit,
matching my stated H1 prior. Since hand-collected rows survive
relevance filtering at ~100%, this would have inflated
confidence-type blockers in the final counts. Corrected by rebalancing
search terms across H1, H2, H3, H0 and neutral framings, with roughly
equal collection from each group. Automated sources (Play Store,
YouTube) are less affected — Play Store is unfiltered by topic, and
YouTube video selection was haul-based rather than size-based, though
the second YouTube pull should be checked for the same problem.

## Hand-collected sample bias, 19 Aug
Hand-collected rows (n=86 before cleaning) are heavily weighted
