## Notable observation, 19 Aug — decluttering video comment
One YouTube comment describes a full non-purchase decision: intent
to buy a black camisole, mentally testing it against existing
wardrobe, recalling a similar item bought a year earlier and never
worn, and deciding against buying. Reason given is neither fit nor
price — it is anticipated non-use based on a remembered previous
failure. Not covered by H1, H2 or H3. Watch for this pattern during
open coding: prior unworn purchases as a blocker on new saves.

